@scene chapter_6_riddle_weaver

background: night_valley.avif
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"West, the land turns strange and soft. Threads of light hang in the air, each strung with tiny glowing runes."
"At the centre of the web a woman works an enormous loom, weaving threads into sentences and unpicking them again."

background: riddle_weaver

npc Riddle Weaver:
"A traveller of letters, letter by letter, arrives —"
"— though not yet lettered enough to read the letters, I'd wager."

npc You:
"...I didn't understand a single word of that."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"No. Not yet. But you will — thread by thread."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE RIDDLE WEAVER"
"Weave a name from the ribbon of runes."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"Words are not LUMPS, child. They are RIBBONS — runes in a row, a line you can cut."

dialogue:
"She plucks a thread from the loom. Runes run along its length, bright and small and ordered."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"Take only the runes you want. A SLICE, from here to there, and the rest falls away."
"Cut the first few runes of a long word, and you may hold a truer name hidden inside it."
"Then do not merely SHOW it, cold and bare. WEAVE it — your own words wrapped snug around the name you found."

dialogue:
"Ahead a final gate stands sealed, a long ribbon of runes across its face."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"The gate hides a name in its first four runes. Slice it loose, then weave it into the words that open the way:"
"'The gate opens for —' and then the name, and a full stop, like a knot tied off."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Slice the first 4 runes as the name, then weave it into: The gate opens for {name}."

mission: riddle_strings

dialogue:
"You cut the first four runes loose — a name, at last — wrap your words around them, and speak."
"The runes rearrange to match, and the gate swings open."

background: night_forest.avif

dialogue:
"Beyond it, far up a leaning tower on the bare rock, a single window burns gold."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"There. Cut, and woven, and spoken true."
"But you have used one motion of the loom, and the loom has many."
"To split a ribbon where it breathes. To join the pieces back. To raise a thread loud, or lay it low."
"And the hardest: to know that a thread once spun can never be recut — only respun."
"Sit. The tower is not going anywhere, and the lazy one up there will expect a weaver, not an apprentice."

dialogue:
"High above, the golden window burns on, patient."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Riddle Weaver"
"Applied: string slicing · f-strings"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 50
achievement: WEAVER OF NAMES

next:
chapter_6b_loom_of_words
